('nizami street + heydar aliyev centre',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','35',35,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving from Hotel to Nizami Street Walking Tour    • One of the city’s main pedestrian streets known for shopping, cafés, and historic architecture.  Popular walking area with boutiques, souvenir shops, and local restaurants.   13:00 – Lunch Break   14:00 – Visit Heydar Aliyev Centre  - You begin exploring the Heydar Aliyev Centre, a world-renowned masterpiece designed by architect Zaha Hadid. The building’s flowing, curved design creates a striking contrast to the surrounding cityscape, making it one of Baku’s most photographed structures. Inside, you may visit the museum halls, cultural exhibitions, and art installations that reflect Azerbaijan’s heritage and contemporary creativity. The vast open spaces, modern gallery designs, and innovative displays offer both visual and cultural insight, while the exterior grounds provide excellent photo opportunities.    18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)   19:00 –Drop to Hotel   Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',35.0),
